  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Monday)\nIssued at 100 PM MDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery shows upper low centered over eastern \nSaskatchewan and western Manitoba with southwest flow across the \nwestern half of the country. Shortwave trough and mid- level \nmoisture plume is evident over the Four Corners region. Surface \nlow pressure is centered over southeastern Saskatchewan with a \ncold front stretching from northern MN through western IA.\n\nCooler today (80s-90 on the plains with 70s to near 80 in the \nBlack Hills) and dry with elevated fire weather the main concern.\nWater vapor imagery highlights upper level moisture pushing into \nthe southern forecast area ahead of the shortwave trough to our \nsouthwest. This wave will bring showers and storms to the area \nlate tonight/early Tuesday morning through Tuesday afternoon. \nWhile widespread severe weather is not expected, a few strong to \nsevere storms are possible across south-central SD into south- \neastern SD Tuesday.\n\nUpper level ridge will build across the Northern Plains Wednesday \nthrough the end of the week with much hotter and drier weather. \nHighs will push into the 90s to near 100 by Friday (on the \nplains). Stronger southerly winds will develop during this time, \nresulting in near-critical to critical fire weather conditions \nWednesday through at least Friday.",
